 "literal": "Profit having-weighed affection who-speak character-without women's motive having-weighed without-associating abandon.",
 "translation": "Weigh the true motives of characterless women who speak words of affection only after weighing their profit, and abandon them without associating with them.",
 "modern": "தமக்குக் கிடைக்கும் பொருளைக் கணக்கிட்டு அன்பாகப் பேசும் பண்பில்லாத பெண்களின் உண்மையான நோக்கத்தை ஆராய்ந்து, அவர்களோடு உறவு கொள்ளாமல் விட்டுவிட வேண்டும்.",
 "explanation": "This couplet warns against women who feign affection purely for financial gain. The word 'பயன்' (profit) reveals their primary motivation, while 'பண்பு' (affection or good quality) is what they falsely project to their suitors. The poet uses a clever contrast between the 'பண்பு' they speak and their actual state of being 'பண்பின்' (without character). By weighing ('தூக்கி') their true motives just as carefully as they weigh their profit, one should avoid their company entirely.",
